{
 "what": "Real beatgrids produced by this build's detector (ANALYSIS_VERSION 4) on real tracks, read out of the local track_analysis cache. Metron's sync probe synthesises grids that are correct by construction; these are not.",
 "why": "A synthetic constant grid makes localTempoDev identically 0, so the feed-forward has nothing to predict and the phase loop's job is trivial. Every one of these carries per-beat jitter instead, which is what the loop actually consumes in production.",
 "caveat": "The jitter is MEASURED, its CAUSE is not. On machine-sequenced 128.00 bpm material a 4.4% swing in a single inter-beat interval (~20 ms) is far more likely beat-tracker resolution than performance rubato, but nothing here establishes that. Do not read these as ground truth for where the beats really are — read them as what the engine is really handed.",
